<title>USA: Aurora completes purchase of Kraft syrup business.</title>
<headline>Aurora completes purchase of Kraft syrup business.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Aurora Foods Inc said Wednesday it had completed the purchase of the Log Cabin syrup business from Kraft Foods Inc for $220 million.</p>
<p>Aurora, formerly known as MBW Foods Inc, said in a statement the retail syrup business was marketed under the Log Cabin and Wigwam brand names.</p>
<p>Private equity investment firm McCown De Leeuw &amp; Co is the majority shareholder of Aurora, which is based in Columbus, Ohio.</p>
<p>Kraft is a unit of Philip Morris Cos Inc.</p>
</text>
